## Press Conference vs. General Conference

A press conference and a general corporate conference need different things from AV. A conference with breakout rooms needs multiple simultaneous setups: see our guide to [audio visual rental for conferences](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-conferences/). A press conference is usually one room, one podium, one speaker or panel addressing the media, with PA sound built to reach the back of the room where press recorders sit.

Our [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers a smaller press conference: a gooseneck microphone for the podium, a projector and screen, up to 40 guests. Our [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers a larger one: a gooseneck and wireless handheld microphone, a 60 inch LED display, a technician included on site, and staging or a lectern available as add ons for the podium.

<InlineCTA />

## What We Provide, and What We Don't

We provide the podium microphone, PA sound, a screen for branding or slides, and staging as an add on for a riser or podium platform. We do not provide cameras, a broadcast or streaming feed, or a press mult box to distribute audio to reporters' own recorders: press typically bring and manage their own recording equipment, and coordinating individual media feeds is between you and the attending press.

A branded backdrop or step-and-repeat banner is also not something we supply: that is usually sourced through your PR or marketing team, positioned behind the podium we set up.

