## FAQs

### What AV equipment do I need for a press conference?

A podium microphone, PA sound that reaches the room, and a screen for branding or slides. The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers a smaller press conference; the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers a larger one with a technician included. See [Press Conference vs. General Conference](#press-conference-vs-general-conference) above.

### Do you provide a camera riser or platform for press photographers?

We don't supply cameras, but our staging add on on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) can be positioned as a riser or platform for photographers and camera operators.

### How many microphones do I need for a press conference?

The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) includes 1 gooseneck microphone for the podium. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a gooseneck plus a wireless handheld microphone, useful if a panel of speakers or a Q&A needs to pass the mic around.

### Do you provide a press mult box or individual audio feeds for reporters?

No, a mult box to distribute the podium audio to multiple reporters' recorders is not part of our catalog. Press typically bring and manage their own recording equipment at the podium.

### Does the AV company provide a branded backdrop or step-and-repeat banner?

No, a backdrop or banner is usually sourced through your PR or marketing team. We set up the podium, sound and staging it stands in front of.

### Do you provide live streaming, broadcast feed or video recording?

No, we do not provide cameras, streaming or broadcast equipment. Our setup covers the room's sound, screen and staging.

### How far in advance should I book AV equipment for a press conference?

Book at least 24 hours in advance to guarantee availability. Our services are available in Malaga and extend to Granada for rentals over 400 euros.

### How many people can a press conference AV setup accommodate?

The Basic MICE Pack covers up to 40 guests, and the MICE Pack covers up to 120.
